# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file.
version: v1.25.0
# Test code is excluded from scanning: its fake HTTP servers echo requests and its scripts open
# paths from their own arguments by design; none of it ships. Production code is always scanned.
exclude:
  global:
    - "**/*_test.go"
    - tests/**
ignore:
  SNYK-CC-TF-73:
    - 'deploy/terraform/aws/main.tf > *':
        reason: >-
          Node egress to 0.0.0.0/0 is limited to the ports a container host needs (443/80 for
          registries and packages, 53 DNS, 123 NTP, 51821 WireGuard); all other egress is VPC-only.
          Registries are chosen by users, so destination CIDRs cannot be enumerated.
        expires: 2027-03-31T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z
  'snyk:lic:golang:github.com:hashicorp:raft:MPL-2.0':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft that is compatible with the project's MIT license: ziroctl
          uses HashiCorp's Raft libraries unmodified, and their source stays available upstream. A change
          to one of these files must be published under MPL-2.0 (community/CONTRIBUTING.md, Dependencies).
        expires: 2027-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
  'snyk:lic:golang:github.com:hashicorp:raft-boltdb:v2:MPL-2.0':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft that is compatible with the project's MIT license: ziroctl
          uses HashiCorp's Raft libraries unmodified, and their source stays available upstream. A change
          to one of these files must be published under MPL-2.0 (community/CONTRIBUTING.md, Dependencies).
        expires: 2027-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
  'snyk:lic:golang:github.com:hashicorp:golang-lru:MPL-2.0':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft that is compatible with the project's MIT license: ziroctl
          uses HashiCorp's Raft libraries unmodified, and their source stays available upstream. A change
          to one of these files must be published under MPL-2.0 (community/CONTRIBUTING.md, Dependencies).
        expires: 2027-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
  'snyk:lic:golang:github.com:hashicorp:go-immutable-radix:MPL-2.0':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          MPL-2.0 is a file-level copyleft that is compatible with the project's MIT license: ziroctl
          uses HashiCorp's Raft libraries unmodified, and their source stays available upstream. A change
          to one of these files must be published under MPL-2.0 (community/CONTRIBUTING.md, Dependencies).
        expires: 2027-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z
  # Snyk Code findings reviewed on 2026-11-27. Rule ids are Snyk Code's (<language>/<rule>); the path limits each entry.
  javascript/DOMXSS:
    - 'tools/ziroctl/cmd/ui/app.js':
        reason: >-
          False positive: the toast text is set with textContent (never parsed as HTML), and element
          children are added with insertAdjacentText, so an error message cannot inject markup.
        expires: 2027-05-27T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z
  go/Ssrf:
    - 'tools/ziroctl/cmd/sandbox.go':
        reason: >-
          False positive: the image name only selects a snapshot already listed by the host's own image store
          (findSnapshot compares it to that list and a fixed pattern) or passes the image policy. Requests to
          other nodes go to mesh addresses taken from cluster state, never from request input; the image is only
          a URL-encoded query value there.
        expires: 2027-05-27T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z
  go/XSS:
    - 'tools/ziroctl/cmd/sandbox_cluster_api.go':
        reason: >-
          Node replies are relayed by relayNodeReply: the body must be valid JSON, the type is application/json
          and X-Content-Type-Options is nosniff, so a browser never renders it as a page. Nodes are cluster peers
          authenticated with the mesh token.
        expires: 2027-05-27T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z
